 ## Overview
-This method optimizes the scalar weight factors $w_{k,j}$ for pre-computed SGGX lobe shapes in volume rendering by minimizing a restricted mean squared error between the rendered and target images. It differs from direct per-voxel optimization by clustering voxels to share weight factors, reducing the parameter space, and uses stochastic gradient descent (SGD) with unbiased gradient estimates obtained via path tracing [S1]. It builds on [Restricted Mean Error Metric](16552-restricted-mean-error-metric.md) by defining the specific error function $E_{L2}$ and the optimization procedure to minimize it.
+This method optimizes the scalar weight factors $w_{k,j}$ for pre-computed SGGX lobe shapes in volume rendering by minimizing a restricted mean squared error between the rendered and target images [S1]. It differs from direct per-voxel optimization by clustering voxels to share weight factors, reducing the parameter space, and uses stochastic gradient descent (SGD) with unbiased gradient estimates obtained via path tracing [S1]. It builds on [Restricted Mean Error Metric](16552-restricted-mean-error-metric.md) by defining the specific error function $E_{L2}$ and the optimization procedure to minimize it [S1].
 
 ## How it works
 **Inputs and Outputs:**
-- **Inputs:** A set of $K$ voxel clusters. For each cluster $k$, a set of $m$ pre-computed lobe shapes $f_{k,j}$ (where $j=1,\dots,m$). Target image intensities $I_r$ for a set of camera rays $r$. Coefficients $c_r$ for each ray.
-- **Outputs:** Optimized weight factors $w_{k,j}$ for each cluster $k$ and lobe $j$.
